WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.400
(audience cheers)

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.010
- You're so loved, I love it!

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.123
Okay, so 16 years ago, I was on your show!

00:00:06.123 --> 00:00:06.956
- [Sharon] Yes!
- I remember!

00:00:06.956 --> 00:00:07.789
With Kelly!
- [Sharon] Yes!

00:00:07.789 --> 00:00:08.750
- I was actually, your
daughter was on there

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:09.750
at the same time.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.140
And now you're on my show.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.791
This is like a full-circle moment!

00:00:12.791 --> 00:00:14.467
(audience cheers)

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:15.513
That's crazy!

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.520
- When I heard that you
were getting your show,

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.193
and it was a daytime show, I was like,

00:00:22.193 --> 00:00:23.830
"Aw, that's fantastic!"

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.530
Just to see the way you've grown,

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.840
and all the different things
that you've been doing

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:28.950
with your career.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.837
And I'm like, "Aw, I wish
I could be on that show."

00:00:31.837 --> 00:00:34.070
"But they'll never ask me because-"

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:34.944
- What?

00:00:34.944 --> 00:00:39.160
- It's a kind of unwritten rule in TV,

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.260
that if you're in the same
kind of space in daytime

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.740
and there's another talk
show on another network,

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:51.740
they don't like to promote
each other's shows.

00:00:51.864 --> 00:00:52.697
- That ain't me.

00:00:52.697 --> 00:00:55.770
- So say, if I wanted to go
on another daytime talk show,

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.027
there's no way, because they'll go,

00:00:57.027 --> 00:00:59.970
"No, you're competition!
You're not coming here."

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.750
And also, there are a few
people that get celebrities

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.650
and they say, "No, you have
to come to my show first."

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.128
So there's all these little things.

00:01:08.128 --> 00:01:09.103
- Political.

00:01:09.103 --> 00:01:10.616
- Always.
- Yeah.

00:01:10.616 --> 00:01:11.970
- And then when you asked me,

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:15.360
I was like, "Oh my god. Trust Kelly!"

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.193
- I love you!

00:01:16.193 --> 00:01:17.463
(audience cheers)

00:01:17.463 --> 00:01:18.833
I don't care where you are!

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.680
- It's like, you have
broken, do you realize

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.987
you have broken the mold by doing that?

00:01:26.987 --> 00:01:28.098
- I didn't actually know!

00:01:28.098 --> 00:01:29.067
(laughter)

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.380
- Because daytime never, never does it!

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.410
- This always happens to me.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:33.380
Like in music, as well.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:34.910
They're always like, surprised.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:37.377
I hate when I get tweets
of like, "Oh my god!"

00:01:37.377 --> 00:01:39.620
"I can't believe she supported
another woman in music!"

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.640
And I'm like, "I'm actually more mad

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.340
at the fact that you have to say that."

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:47.140
- It's great to cross over and
do different things together

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.780
on different people's shows.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:49.613
- 100%!

00:01:49.613 --> 00:01:51.225
- Then you go back and do, now
you have to come on The Talk!

00:01:51.225 --> 00:01:53.410
- Yeah, I was like, "I wanna do The Talk!"

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:55.284
I was like, "You better invite
me after that conversation!"

00:01:55.284 --> 00:01:56.687
- Yes, that's it!

00:01:56.687 --> 00:01:58.060
- No, I love it.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.350
And speaking of The Talk though,

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.650
this is like 10 seasons now?

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:01.900
10 seasons?

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:03.782
- 10 years!
(applause)

00:02:03.782 --> 00:02:05.277
Can you believe it?

00:02:05.277 --> 00:02:07.510
I keep saying this because it's true,

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:09.000
it's the only show I've found

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.523
that I've never got fired from!

00:02:10.523 --> 00:02:12.703
(laughter)
It's true!

00:02:12.703 --> 00:02:16.140
Every show I've ever done, I get the boot!

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.300
- What! Oh my god!

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.180
You're literally one of my
favorite people on the planet.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.430
I can't believe someone would fire!

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.890
You're fired because they can't handle it.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.325
- I don't know!

00:02:23.325 --> 00:02:25.170
- They can't handle the
awesomeness, they can't handle it.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.098
That's what I'm going with.

00:02:26.098 --> 00:02:27.390
- I'll stick with that.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.290
- Exactly!
That's what I do in life.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.560
- Yeah!
- I just filter everything.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.490
They're like, "You're an ugly troll!"

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:32.800
And I'm like, "I'm a beautiful Beyoncé!"

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.418
Thank you, thank you!

00:02:34.418 --> 00:02:36.743
(audience cheers)

00:02:36.743 --> 00:02:37.660
I just filter everything!

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:41.570
But after 10 seasons, I'm
curious, because I keep talking

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.309
to all these hosts about, you
know, their favorite moments.

00:02:43.309 --> 00:02:45.350
And I'm wondering- what's
your favorite moment?

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.360
In 10 seasons, that's a lot of seasons.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.480
- Hmm, my lord.
So.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.510
Well, favorite people.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.543
I know my favorite people

00:02:52.543 --> 00:02:55.120
that I've been allowed to interview.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.610
Is Elton John.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:57.443
- [Kelly] That's a good one.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.763
- [Sharon] And Keanu Reeves.

00:02:58.763 --> 00:03:00.197
- [Kelly] Oh, I love Keanu Reeves!

00:03:00.197 --> 00:03:02.770
- [Sharon] Aw, he's just the best!

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.240
I love him!

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.700
- Yeah, he seems so game.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:06.533
- Oh, he's such a good guy.

00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:07.620
- Actually Elton seems game!

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.930
- Oh yeah, he'll, for a
laugh, he'll do anything.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:13.380
He's so open, too.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.260
- I love this!

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.380
That's why I love you, so much!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.944
I'm gonna keep saying that
like a stalker, I'm sorry.

00:03:16.944 --> 00:03:18.380
(laughter)

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.740
But where there ever any moments,

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.340
because I have these moments on tour

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.300
that I have that didn't go so well.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.100
But did you ever have
any moments on the show

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.307
that you're like, "Mmm,
that didn't go as planned."

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.968
- Oh, yeah!
(laughter)

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:33.810
They used to get me to
do cooking segments,

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:37.555
and I have false nails, and I
stick them on there, you know.

00:03:37.555 --> 00:03:38.388
- Oh, me too!

00:03:38.388 --> 00:03:39.296
- The old, rip off the
back and stick them on.

00:03:39.296 --> 00:03:40.727
- These are stuck on!

00:03:40.727 --> 00:03:41.810
- Woo!
- Yes!

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:46.155
Oh they're even the same color,
we have so much in common.

00:03:46.155 --> 00:03:47.460
(laughter)

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.647
- I would do cooking
segments, and they're like,

00:03:49.647 --> 00:03:52.480
"Get this mince, roll
it up into a burger."

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.503
And I'm rolling it up, and
there's a couple of nails

00:03:55.503 --> 00:03:56.510
(laughter)
in the burger.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:58.540
And I'm like, "Oh, they'll never see it!"

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:01.770
Of course, you know,
like our color shows up.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.727
And Wolfgang didn't really like that.

00:04:04.727 --> 00:04:05.560
(laughter)

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.064
- Oh my god, but it's funny!

00:04:07.064 --> 00:04:07.897
- Yeah!

00:04:07.897 --> 00:04:09.910
- That's the best kind of
television- the unplanned!

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:14.107
- And then, I sat talking
on the show, and I was like,

00:04:14.107 --> 00:04:16.910
"Oh my gosh, there's something
going on in my mouth!"

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.625
And my tooth fell out!

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:20.020
(audience gasps)

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.350
Honestly, I'm not lying.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:22.630
- Like in a cooking demo?

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.230
- [Sharon] No, just sat talking!

00:04:25.644 --> 00:04:27.087
It fell out!
(audience gasps)

00:04:27.087 --> 00:04:28.710
- Did you find it?

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:29.960
- Yeah, it was in my hand!
(laughter)

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.180
- It just?
- Yeah!

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.520
And then, and then, the
guy that runs our show,

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.957
John Redman goes to me in the break,

00:04:36.957 --> 00:04:39.787
"Get some super glue and put it back in!"

00:04:39.787 --> 00:04:41.077
I'm like, "But it won't work!"

00:04:41.077 --> 00:04:43.530
And I've tried the super
glue and everything.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.465
Nothing.

00:04:44.465 --> 00:04:45.930
- I don't know if superglue
should go in your mouth!

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.620
- It didn't even stick it!

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.914
- It didn't even stick anyway?

00:04:48.914 --> 00:04:49.747
- No!

00:04:49.747 --> 00:04:52.258
And it says it sticks anything,
but it doesn't stick teeth!

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.091
(laughter)

00:04:53.091 --> 00:04:54.612
- You needed like,
Gorilla Glue or Duct tape!

00:04:54.612 --> 00:04:58.370
Gorilla glue or Duct tape,
just to get it in there!

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.510
I love that like, did you
just keep doing the show?

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:01.343
- Oh, yeah.

00:05:01.343 --> 00:05:02.595
Just, I went on.
- I love you!

00:05:02.595 --> 00:05:04.043
(claps)

00:05:04.043 --> 00:05:05.441
That's amazing!
- I don't know!

00:05:05.441 --> 00:05:10.370
- So, you've done so many
shows, and I love them all.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.930
But do you ever, are
you ever gonna retire?

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:13.763
Or you love it?

00:05:13.763 --> 00:05:14.596
You just still love it?

00:05:14.596 --> 00:05:18.100
- Yeah, I, you know... it's like,

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:21.530
it gives me such joy, sitting here.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.570
- Yeah.
- This lot with you!

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:28.570
Why would I give up being
able to meet amazing people?

00:05:28.633 --> 00:05:30.048
(applause)

00:05:30.048 --> 00:05:31.034
- That's how I feel!

00:05:31.034 --> 00:05:34.460
- Yeah, and so it's like, if
you're a people person like us,

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:37.700
and somebody says you can't do it anymore,

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:41.080
it would be like, "Then
what am I doing here?"

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:41.913
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:05:41.913 --> 00:05:42.746
- I love that!

00:05:42.746 --> 00:05:43.766
You find joy in it.

00:05:43.766 --> 00:05:44.889
- Yeah. I love it.

00:05:44.889 --> 00:05:46.070
- Yeah, that's why I continue.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:49.010
And it's also why, you're like,
you've done a lot of things.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.400
I do a lot of things because
I get bored with monotony.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:52.513
But I love people. So I'm glad you're-

00:05:52.513 --> 00:05:55.980
- Well I just love
watching you on that Voice,

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:57.139
having a go at everyone!

00:05:57.139 --> 00:05:58.925
(audience cheers)

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:00.425
That gives me joy!

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.240
- I so want you to be
a coach on The Voice!

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:06.700
Because I have seen you on other shows,

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.080
and you are so fantastic!

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.100
Or "fabulous," as you say all the time.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.210
I'm seriously a stalker.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.290
I've watched so many.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.029
But here's one thing I love that you did.

00:06:15.029 --> 00:06:16.340
I think you actually did it

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.390
the beginning of The Talk this season.

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.720
You talked openly about face lifts.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:20.960
- Yeah.
- You've talked openly.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.850
It almost makes it less
taboo and less of a topic,

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:24.683
if you do.

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:25.860
That's what I love about Dolly Parton.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.693
She owns every bit of it.

00:06:26.693 --> 00:06:27.870
- [Sharon] Oh, sure!
- She's like, "Yeah!"

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.167
- Everything!
Yeah, yeah!

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:30.410
- But I love that you do that.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.020
Because, while some people
might not be comfortable

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:34.410
with that, some people
are comfortable with that!

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.640
And that's why they love to do it!

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.473
- Yeah!

00:06:36.473 --> 00:06:37.610
- And I love that you
talk about it openly,

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:38.580
because a lot of people don't.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.467
And they're like, "I
haven't had anything done!"

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:41.990
- This is just a new cream!

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:43.250
(audience laughs)

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.635
- [Kelly] It's my new cream!

00:06:44.635 --> 00:06:46.830
- Yes, try this cream!

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:49.110
It lifts everything overnight!

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:50.547
- Lies and deception!

00:06:50.547 --> 00:06:51.380
- I know!

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:53.439
It's like, oh please!

00:06:53.439 --> 00:06:55.026
(laughter)

00:06:55.026 --> 00:06:55.859
- Is it hard?

00:06:55.859 --> 00:06:57.260
Because I'm scared of stuff like that.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:58.093
I'm terrified.

00:06:58.093 --> 00:06:59.670
Like, I can get tattoos.
I have like 15.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.190
But the thought of something-
I'm scared of this.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.080
You're never scared?

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.330
You just go in and you're like, "Yeah."

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.650
- I am, I am.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:05.483
Yeah, sure.

00:07:05.483 --> 00:07:08.310
Because you know, you could
wake up and look like Cyclops,

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:09.810
you never know.

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:13.720
And like, I have this thing
where they lifted up my mouth.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:16.770
And then for the first week, I'm like,

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:17.910
I couldn't feel my mouth.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:20.857
I can hardly feel my mouth
now, to be honest with you!

00:07:20.857 --> 00:07:22.340
(laughter and applause)

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.170
It's- I couldn't find my mouth!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.431
- It can be handy in certain situations.

00:07:26.431 --> 00:07:27.264
- Yes!
- Okay.

00:07:27.264 --> 00:07:31.050
- But it's like, all numb,
and I had it- it was up

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.282
on one side, and I looked like Elvis.

00:07:33.282 --> 00:07:35.887
And all the kids and Ozzy are going,

00:07:35.887 --> 00:07:37.350
"Why are you snarling at me?"

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:39.067
I'm like, "I'm not snarling!"

00:07:39.067 --> 00:07:40.400
"I'm not doing anything!"

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.233
(laughter)

00:07:41.233 --> 00:07:42.066
But it was this!

00:07:42.066 --> 00:07:43.875
It was going up like!

00:07:43.875 --> 00:07:45.930
- My mother had dental work done one time,

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.390
and I felt so bad because, it literally,

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:48.810
she couldn't feel it
because they numbed it.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:49.643
- [Sharon] Yeah!

00:07:49.643 --> 00:07:50.476
- And we were eating,

00:07:50.476 --> 00:07:52.360
and her spaghetti was
coming out of her mouth.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.860
And I couldn't tell her
because I was laughing so hard,

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.240
and she was getting so mad at me.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.817
And then she just kept going "Ha, ha!"

00:07:58.869 --> 00:08:01.660
And I was like, "It's getting
worse, mom! It's awesome!"

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.250
Anyway, I love you for being open.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:05.300
That's one of the reasons why I love you.

